    "text": "A cylindrical cavity of diameter a exists inside a cylinder of diameter <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>a</mi></math> as shown in the figure. Both the cylinder and the cavity are infinity long. A uniform current density&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>J</mi></math> flows along the length. If the magnitude of the magnetic field at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">N</mtext><mrow><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>a</mi><mtext mathvariant=\"italic\">J</mtext></math>, then the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math> is<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/EM0012130_Ques1_1.jpg\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 197px;\" />",
